From: hashtagbasit
Subject: tty: serial: qcom-geni: release a port's CX and bus votes across system suspend

An open geni UART keeps the performance level its clock rate needs on the CX
rail (dev_pm_opp_set_rate() with the port's rate) and its interconnect
bandwidth for as long as it is open. Nothing drops either for system suspend:
only the console's bandwidth vote is switched to active-only. On a Pocket FIT
three ports stay open all the time (Bluetooth, the controller MCU and the
debug console), and their levels (128, 64 and 64) are still voted while the
system sleeps, so RPMh never collapses CX: the cxsd, aosd and ddr sleep
counters stayed at 0 through every s2idle, even with sync_state forced and
the USB and PCIe controllers unbound.

The port is stopped by then (uart_suspend_port() has run, and these UARTs are
not wakeup sources), so after it let go of the performance level and make the
bandwidth vote active-only for every port, the way the console already does,
and put both back before uart_resume_port() starts it again.

---
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
@@ -1983,6 +1983,7 @@
 	struct qcom_geni_serial_port *port = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	struct uart_port *uport = &port->uport;
 	struct qcom_geni_private_data *private_data = uport->private_data;
+	int ret;
 
 	/*
 	 * A peer that keeps streaming into a non-console geni UART across the
@@ -2000,16 +2001,25 @@
 	 */
 	if (!uart_console(uport))
 		disable_irq(uport->irq);
+
+	ret = uart_suspend_port(private_data->drv, uport);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 
 	/*
-	 * This is done so we can hit the lowest possible state in suspend
-	 * even with no_console_suspend
+	 * An open port still votes its CX level and bus bandwidth here, and
+	 * those stay in RPMh's sleep set: any open UART keeps the SoC out of
+	 * CX collapse. Leave nothing voted while the system sleeps (the port
+	 * is stopped), for every port, not only the console. Bandwidth stays
+	 * up while the CPUs run, so a console with no_console_suspend still
+	 * prints.
 	 */
-	if (uart_console(uport)) {
-		geni_icc_set_tag(&port->se, QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY);
-		geni_icc_set_bw(&port->se);
-	}
-	return uart_suspend_port(private_data->drv, uport);
+	geni_icc_set_tag(&port->se, QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY);
+	geni_icc_set_bw(&port->se);
+	if (port->clk_rate)
+		dev_pm_opp_set_rate(dev, 0);
+
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int qcom_geni_serial_resume(struct device *dev)
@@ -2019,14 +2029,16 @@
 	struct uart_port *uport = &port->uport;
 	struct qcom_geni_private_data *private_data = uport->private_data;
 
+	/* Votes back before the port runs again (see qcom_geni_serial_suspend()). */
+	if (port->clk_rate)
+		dev_pm_opp_set_rate(dev, port->clk_rate);
+	geni_icc_set_tag(&port->se, QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS);
+	geni_icc_set_bw(&port->se);
+
 	ret = uart_resume_port(private_data->drv, uport);
 	/* Balance the disable_irq() taken in qcom_geni_serial_suspend(). */
 	if (!uart_console(uport))
 		enable_irq(uport->irq);
-	if (uart_console(uport)) {
-		geni_icc_set_tag(&port->se, QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS);
-		geni_icc_set_bw(&port->se);
-	}
 	return ret;
 }
 
